      "prompt": "\n\nThe following skills provide specialized instructions for specific tasks.\nUse the read tool to load a skill's file when the task matches its description.\nWhen a skill file references a relative path, resolve it against the skill directory (parent of SKILL.md / dirname of the path) and use that absolute path in tool commands.\n\n<available_skills>\n  <skill>\n    <name>ask-data-in-natural-language</name>\n    <description>智能问数技能 - 对文件夹中的Excel/CSV数据进行自然语言问答，自动编写pandas代码进行统计分析，回答用户关于运营数据的统计问题。使用这个技能当用户想用自然语言询问数据问题、分析DWS/知聊/知识库/智能体平台等产品的运营数据时。</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/ask-data-in-natural-language/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>contact-book</name>\n    <description>通讯录查询</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/contact-book/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>customer-complaint-inspection-skill</name>\n    <description>本技能用于对客户投诉处理情况报告文件内容进行审核质检。严格依据内置规则，对客户投诉处理情况报告进行逐项合规质检。当需要根据原始投诉内容校验客户投诉处理情况报告完整性、准确性及逻辑一致性时，使用本技能。</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/customer-complaint-inspection-skill/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>data-analyst</name>\n    <description>Data visualization, report generation, SQL queries, and spreadsheet automation. Transform your AI agent into a data-savvy analyst that turns raw data into actionable insights.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/data-analyst/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>docx</name>\n    <description>Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, read, edit, or manipulate Word documents (.docx files). Triggers include: any mention of &apos;Word doc&apos;, &apos;word document&apos;, &apos;.docx&apos;, or requests to produce professional documents with formatting like tables of contents, headings, page numbers, or letterheads. Also use when extracting or reorganizing content from .docx files, inserting or replacing images in documents, performing find-and-replace in Word files, working with tracked changes or comments, or converting content into a polished Word document. If the user asks for a &apos;report&apos;, &apos;memo&apos;, &apos;letter&apos;, &apos;template&apos;, or similar deliverable as a Word or .docx file, use this skill. Do NOT use for PDFs, spreadsheets, Google Docs, or general coding tasks unrelated to document generation. IMPORTANT: After generating a .docx file, you MUST proactively ask the user whether they want to upload it to their personal knowledge base. If they say yes, load and invoke the km-operation-prod skill to upload the file.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/docx/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>emailme</name>\n    <description>This skill should be used when the user wants to send an email to themselves via the internal mail system. It invokes the local binary sendmeprod-static to deliver emails (with optional attachments) to the user&apos;s own internal mailbox. Use this skill whenever the user asks to send me an email, mail me the results, email the report to me, or any similar request that implies delivering content to the user&apos;s personal inbox.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/emailme/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>fetch-news</name>\n    <description>爬取公司内部动态并支持问答检索。当用户需要获取公司内部动态、爬取内网门户和集团门户资讯，或对已爬取的资讯进行问答检索时必须使用此技能。包括用户提到&quot;内部动态&quot;、&quot;内网资讯&quot;、&quot;今日新闻&quot;、&quot;集团动态&quot;、&quot;媒体报道&quot;、&quot;党史学习教育&quot;、&quot;党史&quot;、&quot;八项规定&quot;、&quot;八项规定精神&quot;、&quot;国寿动态&quot;、&quot;通知公告&quot;、&quot;分支机构&quot;、&quot;公关宣传&quot;、&quot;每日更新&quot;等关键词时都应触发此技能。支持按日期筛选（今天、昨天、这周等）和分类检索。</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/fetch-news/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>insurance-product-qa</name>\n    <description>保险产品问答skill，调用外部SSE流式接口处理保险产品相关问题。当用户询问保险产品相关问题，如产品责任、保障范围、产品区别、适用人群等问题时使用此skill。特别适用于处理&quot;康宁尊享重大疾病保险对象、保险责任是什么？&quot;、&quot;哪些产品能保阿尔兹海默症&quot;、&quot;72岁能买哪些医疗险&quot;、&quot;鑫鸿福分红型和鑫鸿福分红型典藏版有什么区别&quot;等类型的保险产品问答。此skill调用外部知识管理平台的SSE流式问答接口，需要配置USER.md中的kmBaseUrl。</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/insurance-product-qa/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>km-operation-prod</name>\n    <description>This skill MUST be used whenever the user mentions &quot;文件上传&quot;, &quot;上传文件&quot;, &quot;upload file&quot;, &quot;上传到KM&quot;, &quot;上传到知识库&quot;, &quot;上传到知识管理平台&quot;, or any request to upload a document to the KM knowledge management platform (km.clic / test.km.clic). Also handles file download and directory queries on the KM platform. Uses curl-based shell scripts — no Node.js packages required.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/km-operation-prod/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>nickname-lobster-call</name>\n    <description>自定义用户昵称和对龙虾 AI 的称呼。当用户说&quot;以后叫我 XX&quot;、&quot;我想改名字&quot;、&quot;你叫什么&quot;、&quot;我该怎么称呼你&quot;、&quot;查看我的昵称&quot;、&quot;给你起个新名字&quot;、&quot;换昵称&quot;时必须触发此技能。支持保存昵称、修改 AI 称呼、查询当前设置，提升交互亲切感。</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/nickname-lobster-call/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>official-doc-writer</name>\n    <description>党政机关公文生成技能，支持通知、报告、请示、函等公文类型，符合GB/T 9704-2012标准。当用户需要生成党政机关公文、创建正式文件、导出Word格式公文时调用。无论用户使用何种表述方式（如&apos;帮我写个报告&apos;、&apos;生成一份通知&apos;、&apos;制作公文&apos;等），只要涉及公文文档生成，都应使用此技能。</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/official-doc-writer/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>pdf</name>\n    <description>Use this skill whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files. This includes reading or extracting text/tables from PDFs, combining or merging multiple PDFs into one, splitting PDFs apart, rotating pages, adding watermarks, creating new PDFs, filling PDF forms, encrypting/decrypting PDFs, extracting images, and OCR on scanned PDFs to make them searchable. If the user mentions a .pdf file or asks to produce one, use this skill. IMPORTANT: After generating a PDF file, you MUST proactively ask the user whether they want to upload it to their personal knowledge base. If they say yes, load and invoke the km-operation-prod skill to upload the file.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/pdf/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>pptx</name>\n    <description>Use this skill any time a .pptx file is involved in any way — as input, output, or both. This includes: creating slide decks, pitch decks, or presentations; reading, parsing, or extracting text from any .pptx file (even if the extracted content will be used elsewhere, like in an email or summary); editing, modifying, or updating existing presentations; combining or splitting slide files; working with templates, layouts, speaker notes, or comments. Trigger whenever the user mentions &quot;deck,&quot; &quot;slides,&quot; &quot;presentation,&quot; or references a .pptx filename, regardless of what they plan to do with the content afterward. If a .pptx file needs to be opened, created, or touched, use this skill. IMPORTANT: After generating a .pptx file, you MUST proactively ask the user whether they want to upload it to their personal knowledge base. If they say yes, load and invoke the km-operation-prod skill to upload the file.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/pptx/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>self-improvement</name>\n    <description>Captures learnings, errors, and corrections to enable continuous improvement. Use when: (1) A command or operation fails unexpectedly, (2) User corrects Claude (&apos;No, that&apos;s wrong...&apos;, &apos;Actually...&apos;), (3) User requests a capability that doesn&apos;t exist, (4) An external API or tool fails, (5) Claude realizes its knowledge is outdated or incorrect, (6) A better approach is discovered for a recurring task. Also review learnings before major tasks.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/self-improving-agent/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>skill-creator</name>\n    <description>Create, edit, improve, or audit AgentSkills. Use when creating a new skill from scratch or when asked to improve, review, audit, tidy up, or clean up an existing skill or SKILL.md file. Also use when editing or restructuring a skill directory (moving files to references/ or scripts/, removing stale content, validating against the AgentSkills spec). Triggers on phrases like &quot;create a skill&quot;, &quot;author a skill&quot;, &quot;tidy up a skill&quot;, &quot;improve this skill&quot;, &quot;review the skill&quot;, &quot;clean up the skill&quot;, &quot;audit the skill&quot;.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>skill-vetter</name>\n    <description>Security-first skill vetting for AI agents. Use before installing any skill from ClawdHub, GitHub, or other sources. Checks for red flags, permission scope, and suspicious patterns.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/skill-vetter/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>tender-bid-inspect-skill</name>\n    <description>本技能用于通用招投标文件质检，由模型自行识别文件类型并完成规则构建与质检</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/tender-bid-inspect-skill/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>understand-image</name>\n    <description>本环境已经部署了内部多模态大模型用于图片理解。**你必须使用这个技能来处理所有图片任务**。不管用户是要描述图片、提取文字、分析图表、解读扫描文档、识别截图，只要工作区有图片文件需要理解，都必须调用此技能。**绝对禁止推荐任何外部 OCR 工具（Tesseract、在线服务等）**，这里已经有可用的多模态大模型了。即使只说&quot;看看这张图&quot;也要调用。</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/understand-image/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>xlsx</name>\n    <description>Use this skill any time a spreadsheet file is the primary input or output. This means any task where the user wants to: open, read, edit, or fix an existing .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv, or .tsv file (e.g., adding columns, computing formulas, formatting, charting, cleaning messy data); create a new spreadsheet from scratch or from other data sources; or convert between tabular file formats. Trigger especially when the user references a spreadsheet file by name or path — even casually (like &quot;the xlsx in my downloads&quot;) — and wants something done to it or produced from it. Also trigger for cleaning or restructuring messy tabular data files (malformed rows, misplaced headers, junk data) into proper spreadsheets. The deliverable must be a spreadsheet file. Do NOT trigger when the primary deliverable is a Word document, HTML report, standalone Python script, database pipeline, or Google Sheets API integration, even if tabular data is involved. IMPORTANT: After generating a spreadsheet file, you MUST proactively ask the user whether they want to upload it to their personal knowledge base. If they say yes, load and invoke the km-operation-prod skill to upload the file.</description>\n    <location>/app/skills/xlsx/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n  <skill>\n    <name>imap-smtp-email</name>\n    <description>Read and send email via IMAP/SMTP. Check for new/unread messages, fetch content, search mailboxes, mark as read/unread, and send emails with attachments. Supports multiple accounts. Works with any IMAP/SMTP server including Gmail, Outlook, 163.com, vip.163.com, 126.com, vip.126.com, 188.com, and vip.188.com.</description>\n    <location>~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/imap-smtp-email/SKILL.md</location>\n  </skill>\n</available_skills>",
